# LF everywhere. No OS-specific end-of-line mapping, on any platform.
#
# Every text file is stored LF in the repo AND checked out LF, whatever each
# machine's core.autocrlf happens to be, so Windows and WSL/Linux git agree on
# the state of the work tree.
#
# This matches the policy the code already enforces: infra/file_util.lua
# writeFile opens in binary mode so "\n" stays one byte on every platform, and
# serde/exporter.lua rejects a CR in any exported text file outright. Reading
# CRLF stays tolerated everywhere; only writing and storing it is refused.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Compressed payload: never EOL-translate.
*.gz binary
